export const title = "exacqVision Integration Guide";
export const html = "<h1>exacqVision Integration Guide</h1>\n      <hr class=\"rule\" />\n\n<h2>1. Introduction</h2>\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">1.1 Prerequisites</h3>\n<ul class=\"steps\">\n<li>AIBridge FW version 103708 or greater.</li>\n<li>exacqVision Client 24.06.1.0 or greater.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">1.2 Understanding the Integration Architecture</h3>\n<p>There are two ways to integrate AIBridge with exacqVision VMS.</p>\n<p><strong>1) Case 1</strong> &ndash; AIBridge receives the RTSP video stream from the IP camera, performs AI analysis, and provides an annotated video stream along with event data. The video is transcoded to include object recognition data, bounding boxes, and zone information.</p>\n<p><strong>2) Case 2</strong> &ndash; Both AIBridge and exacqVision VMS receive the RTSP stream from the IP camera at the same time. AIBridge sends only the AI analysis events directly to exacqVision VMS, and can also fetch the RTSP stream from exacqVision VMS instead of receiving it directly from the IP camera.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">Between Case 1 and Case 2, this guide explains integration using Case 1, since annotated video is generally preferred.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h2>2. Configuration</h2>\n<p>Event integration between AI Bridge and exacqVision requires both exacqVision serial port configuration and AI Bridge configuration.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">2.1 exacqVision Configuration</h3>\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:18px;font-size:15px;\">2.1.1 Adding a Device</h4>\n<p>To use annotated video, you must first add a device. If you don't plan to use annotated video, you can skip this section &mdash; but note the video stream must be input into AI Bridge for a device to be added successfully.</p>\n<p>In the exacqVision client, click <strong>Add IP Cameras</strong>, then click <strong>New</strong> to enter the device information and add the device.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">When registering an AI Bridge with 4 or more channels, append <code>#bank=n</code> after the IP address &ndash; for example <code>192.168.77.182</code>, <code>192.168.77.182#bank=2</code>, <code>192.168.77.182#bank=3</code>, <code>192.168.77.182#bank=4</code>.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:18px;font-size:15px;\">2.1.2 Serial Port Setup</h4>\n<p>Once the device is registered, follow these steps to register AI events in exacqVision. In the Serial Ports tab, click <strong>New</strong> and enter a name. Set <strong>Use</strong> to <code>POS</code> and <strong>Profile</strong> to <code>New</code>. Set <strong>Type</strong> to <code>TCP Listener</code>, enter the AI Bridge's IP in the Address field, and enter the port you'll configure on AI Bridge in the Port field. Set Max Line Length and Timeout appropriately, and enter <code>\\x0a</code> in Line Ending. Once complete, click <strong>Apply</strong> &mdash; you'll be taken to the Serial Profile tab automatically.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 6px;\"><code>\\x0a</code> is the hex code for a line break, as specified in the exacqVision manual.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">If an existing profile is available, select it instead of creating a new one.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:18px;font-size:15px;\">2.1.3 Serial Profile Setup</h4>\n<p>In the Serial Profile tab, click <strong>New</strong> and select the port name you created earlier. Enter <code>@Start</code> in the SOT marker field and <code>@End</code> in the EOT marker field, then click <strong>Apply</strong>.</p>\n<p>In the Live Display tab, choose the background video where the message will be shown, then drag within the video to position the message. Font settings can be adjusted under Text Formatting.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">exacqVision only supports a single server port, and only one communication per port, so every event from a single AI Bridge is received on that one port. Because of this, it's recommended to set the serial profile background to <strong>None</strong> rather than a specific channel.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Line Masks lets you add text for data you want to ignore.</p>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:18px;font-size:15px;\">2.1.4 Setting Event Keywords for Event Linking</h4>\n<p>In Serial Profiles, go to the <strong>Event Keywords</strong> section and add channel keywords. In the <strong>Event Linking</strong> tab, register the event action for each channel.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">2.2 AI Bridge Configuration</h3>\n<p>This section covers generating AI Bridge events.</p>\n<p>From the left menu, go to <strong>App Settings &gt; Explore AI Apps</strong> and select the AI feature you want. AIBridge provides over 50 AI applications &mdash; see the full list at the <a href=\"https://indoai.com/goods/catalog?page=1&searchMode=catalog&category=c0006&per=40&sorting=ranking&filter_display=lattice&code=0006\">catalog link</a>. This guide uses Intrusion Detection.</p>\n<p>Click <strong>Add Rule</strong>, add the event setting, configure the zone, then click <strong>Apply</strong>. Add an action setting, choose <strong>exacqVision</strong> as the action type, and check the checkbox.</p>\n\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:340px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:80px 1fr;\">\n    <span>Action Type</span><select disabled><option>exacqVision</option></select>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<p><strong>Edit the exacqVision server settings:</strong> enter the exacqVision server's IP address and the port you created in the serial port setup (section 2.1.2). In the Editable Box, enter the message content you want &mdash; you can use String Construction or add specific token values.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">To link an event to a specific channel in exacqVision, the message must include a field that distinguishes the channel.</p>\n</div>\n<p>After entering the message, click the <strong>Test</strong> button. On success, a \"Completed\" message appears; on failure, an \"Error\" message appears &mdash; check your server settings if this happens.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 6px;\">There are two ways to check whether the server connection succeeded: check the Status in exacqVision's Serial Ports or Serial Profiles.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">If events aren't working as expected, check your firewall settings.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Once everything is configured, click <strong>Apply</strong>. Click the exacqVision setting you just created, then click <strong>Apply</strong> again.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">If too many objects are detected and the message becomes too long, some objects may be truncated.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Finally, click the <strong>Submit</strong> button.</p>\n\n<h2>3. Demo</h2>\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">3.1 Live</h3>\n<p>Live video can be checked from the Live Cameras tab of the exacqVision client.</p>\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">3.2 Recorded Search</h3>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">Selecting multiple videos displays them in a split screen.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h2>4. FAQ</h2>\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">4.1 LPR Group Scenario</h3>\n<p>As shown, using Group mode on an LPR license lets you use AI events more efficiently. Add a group, then add license plate numbers and assign them to the group. Searching Serial for <strong>VIP</strong> shows results based on the group.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">Make sure the Editable Box includes <code>LP_GROUP_NAME</code>.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h2>5. Revision History</h2>\n<ul class=\"steps\">\n<li>v1.00 Initial document creation.</li>\n<li>v1.01 Adding FAQ &ndash; LPR App's Group.</li>\n</ul>";
